Guess the Word — Individual Project (Logic Game, 5–7 hours)
Support for Guess the Word : String and List manipulationLinks to an external site.

Overview
Build a console word-guessing game. The computer chooses a secret word; the player guesses letters. Correct guesses reveal letters; incorrect guesses reduce the number of tries. The game ends when the player reveals the whole word or runs out of tries.

Requirements (must have)
Word Pool

Store a small in-code list of at least 20 words (strings).

Pick one random word each round.

Game Loop

Show progress as underscores and revealed letters (e.g., p _ t h o n).

Prompt the player to enter a single letter.

Track already guessed letters; do not penalize repeats—just warn and reprompt.

If the letter is in the word, reveal all positions; otherwise decrease remaining tries.

Game ends on win (all letters revealed) or when tries reach 0.

Tries & Feedback

Start with 6–10 tries (you choose).

After each guess, print:

the masked word (with spaces between letters),

remaining tries,

sorted list of letters already guessed.

Input Validation

Ignore and reprompt on blank input.

Accept only letters a–z (case-insensitive); convert to lower case internally.

If the user types more than one character or a non-letter, reprompt.

Play Again

After a round ends, ask: “Play again? (y/n)”. Validate and loop accordingly.

Scores 
Keep track of the score of your player.  Wins vs Losses
No Scaffolding

Do not import external files or use starter code. Standard library only (random is fine).

Choose 2:
Difficulty levels (tries 10/8/6 or word length buckets).

Categories (animals, foods, sports) with random pick from the chosen category.

A “hint” that reveals one random unguessed letter (costs 2 tries).

